ch that adds new things you can do in Yapin\u2019. Each one has its own switch:","Save any message and find it again later (Ctrl+Shift+B), give people private notes and nicknames only you can see, and fold away messages from someone you\u2019d rather not read","Copy or quote a message, get reminded about a message later, and turn a message into a picture card to save or share","Find in chat (Ctrl+Shift+L), a quick switcher for channels, servers, saved messages and Studio pages (Ctrl+Shift+K), a picture viewer with zoom, and chat export as text or a web page","Mention alerts, a typing counter on the message box, and saved replies you can drop in with one click","A text styler with 38 styles, a toolbox of 48 little tools (calculator, unit converters, world clock, dice, colour codes and more), hundreds of symbols and text faces, and 30 more colour themes","Pixel Studio gets 37 filters and 24 stamps you can drag into place (Image menu, with Feature+ on)"]],["Better",["Customization+ and Feature+ now live together on one Extras page in the Tools group, each with its own switch","Settings search looks through both Extras pages, and the quick switcher can open either one","Fixed an error when switching off the typing counter, and lots of small layout touches"]]]],["6.6","November 2026","Customization+, cloud saves and a new Pixel Studio",[["New",["Customization+: one switch (in its own tab) that unlocks dozens more styles for Yapin\u2019: message weight, spacing and glow, name styles, hover and mention styles, links, code and reply colours, rounded images, embed and reaction styles, channel and server effects, message box shapes, menus, pop-ups, scrollbars, avatar rings, accessibility options and more","Cloud saves for Pixel Studio: save projects to your Yap++ Studio account and open them on any computer or on the website (make a sync key on yap-studio.pages.dev/account)","Pixel Studio is redesigned: menus, a tool options bar, foldable panels, a colour picker square, rulers, a navigator, a magnifier for picking colours and a History panel where every step has a name","Protect pfp keeps the profile picture area clear on decals, profile effects and name plates, and Perfect circle trims the edge squares on export so the hole is a perfect circle","New tools and brushes: spray, colour replace, contour, custom brushes from a selection, rounded rectangles, selection resize handles, Alt+drag to copy, pattern ink, and (with Customization+) a polygon and star tool, 10 brush shapes, scatter, spacing and spin symmetry","Lots more: blend modes, layer locks and colour tags, drag layers and frames to reorder, 16 new palettes, colour harmony, shaded outlines, posterize, pixelate, colour cycle and bob animation makers, more export options, paste pictures from other apps, two-finger zoom and an Editor settings window"]],["Better",["Drag the view with left click in the empty space round the canvas, or with the hand button","Drawing is smoother on big animated canvases, and tens of thousands of random test actions found nothing broken"]]]],["6.5","November 2026","Games, levelled up",[["New",["Brick Blitz: a new brick breaker with levels and power-ups (wider paddle, extra balls, slow motion)","Every game has sound effects (with a mute button), screen shake, particle bursts and score pop-ups, and real-time games pause with P (or by themselves when you switch away)","Meteor Dodge: shield and slow-mo power-ups. Pixel Serpent: a slow-time potion and rocks that appear as you grow. Stack Tower: a pixel skyline and perfect-drop bonuses","Memory Match cards flip over and you get a star rating; Reaction Rush rates every tap; casino wins rain coins","7 new game achievements, from Arcade rookie to High roller"]]]],["6.4","November 2026","Casino corner and new sizes",[["New",["Casino corner: Lucky Slots, Twenty-One, Higher or Lower, Lucky Wheel and Peg Drop, played with pretend coins (just for fun: nothing real is won or lost)","Pixel Studio: Profile effect (exports at 450 x 880) and Name plate (600 x 120) sizes, with Yapin\u2019s layout drawn on so you know what to keep clear"]]]],["6.3","November 2026","Games and Support me",[["New",["Games: five little pixel games made for Studio (Stack Tower, Pixel Serpent, Meteor Dodge, Memory Match and Reaction Rush), with best scores, keyboard, mouse and touch controls","Support me: see Dexterious\u2019s decals and get them on Yapin\u2019 with shards to support Studio"]]]],["6.2","November 2026","Updates that always work",[["New",["Studio now updates itself on every Yap++, old and new, straight from Yap++ Studio\u2019s own GitHub: one click on Update now and it reloads on the new version"]],["Fixed",["\u201cThis Yap++ is too old to update Studio\u201d: older Yap++ versions can update Studio now"]]]],["6.1","November 2026","Pixel Studio 2",[["New",["Pixel Studio 2: select a box, draw a lasso or use the magic wand, then copy, cut, paste, move, nudge, flip, rotate, crop or invert it. Drawing only happens inside the selection","New tools: dithered gradient, shade (lightens or darkens with a little hue shift), dither brush and pixel text","Pixel-perfect pencil lines, a round brush, and fill every pixel of a colour at once (Shift+click)","Hold Shift for straight and 45-degree lines, squares and circles. Alt+click takes a colour with any tool","Lock a layer\u2019s transparent pixels to paint only over what\u2019s already there","Canvas menu: resize with an anchor, scale 2x, flip, rotate, trim empty edges, crop, add an outline, swap colours","Trace over a picture, a big grid every 8, 16 or 32 pixels, and tile mode for patterns","A live animated preview, a shade ramp for your colour, grab colours from the picture, the colour under the cursor, and a shortcuts list (press ?)"]]]],["6.0","November 2026","Side Chat and a lot more",[["New",["Updates itself: Studio tells you when a new version is out and installs it in place with one click (no installer, settings stay). Updates are signed, so only real Studio updates can install","Android app: Yapin\u2019 with Studio built in, ping notifications even when the app is closed (tap one to jump to the message), quiet hours, and an off switch that really turns them off. Download it from the Yap++ Studio website","Sync code: copy all your settings as one code and paste it on your phone or another computer (Advanced)","On phones: drag the Studio button anywhere, swipe the quick panel down to close it, a little buzz on achievements, and the screen stays on during a focus session","Works on phones (in the browser, from the Yap++ Studio website): Studio fits Yapin\u2019s phone layout, a small Studio button opens the quick panel, and Side Chat fills the screen. Pixel Studio stays on computers and tablets","Side Chat: keep another server's chat open in a small window while you use a different one. Pin up to 6 chats as tabs, drag, resize, minimise to a bubble that counts new messages","A Side Chat button in every channel header, and Ctrl+Shift+D to open or close it","Productivity page: sticky notes (Ctrl+Shift+N), a focus timer with breaks, break reminders and text shortcuts like ;shrug;","Spotlight people: highlight messages from the people you care about","Yap++'s plugin page redesigned: cards with icons, hover glow, search and On / Off filters","Studio redesign: a glow that follows your mouse, a sliding menu highlight, glowing switches and shiny buttons","6 new achievements in a new Productivity group","Presets: Neon Night, Forest Moss, Ocean Deep","Badges: chat bubble, clock, notepad","Quick panel: Side Chat, note and timer buttons, and drawn icons instead of emoji","Pixel Studio: a full pixel art editor for banners, profile pictures, decals and server icons, with layers, shapes, fill, mirror drawing, undo, palettes, saved projects, image import and PNG export at upload size","A new clock: Boxed and Pixel styles, sizes, the date, and drag it anywhere","A redesigned focus timer with Boxed and Pixel styles and a count of your sessions today","The official Yap++ Studio icon, and a Yap++ \xd7 Yap++ Studio loading screen when Yap++ opens (turn it off in Advanced)","A new achievement pop-up, and achievements sorted by rarity","Redesigned Achievements page: your rank, stats, recently unlocked, a reward track, search and sorting","Redesigned Credits page with the full release history","Animation in Pixel Studio: frames with their own timing, onion skin, playback, animated GIF export (with a size check against Yapin's limits), sprite sheets, and opening animated GIFs as frames","My Decals: spot who's wearing the decorations you made as you browse"]]]],["5.0","November 2026","The fun update",[["New",["Fun page: a desk pet ghost you can click, message confetti, click ripples, cursor sparkle trail, typing sparkles","Typing and send sounds made on your PC, with a volume slider","Rainbow accent that cycles your accent colour everywhere","Photo filters: Vivid, Dreamy, Vintage, Sepia, B&W","Achievements page with 15 goals and pop-ups when you unlock one","Your stats on Home","Theme codes: copy your colours as a short code or paste a friend\u2019s","Presets: Galaxy, Matrix, Sunset Beach, Retro Terminal, Strawberry Milk","Badges: sword, pizza, mushroom, bunny, planet, sun","Layout: server icon size, member list width, image size limit, rounded message box","Privacy: blur avatars, hide your status text","Background effects: hearts, bubbles, leaves","Ctrl+Shift+P switches to the next theme preset","This Updates page"]],["Fixed",["Stars and Fireflies backgrounds now twinkle and drift"]]]],["4.0","November 2026","The big redesign",[["New",["New look with a grouped side menu, page headers, search and a master on/off switch","Credits page","Installer with a safety letter"]],["Fixed",["The profile bar no longer moves right and hides a button when frosted panels are on"]]]],["3.0","October 2026","Badges and more",[["New",["Badges page: wear pixel badges, shareable with other Studio users through your bio","Q